-- @description ReaBrowse
-- @version 1.0.0-rc10
-- @author davvolinni-ui
-- @links
--   Support https://forum.cockos.com/showthread.php?p=2958956#post2958956
--   GitHub repository https://github.com/davvolinni-ui/ReaBrowse
-- @about
--   ReaBrowse is an audio, MIDI, FX, instrument, and action browser for REAPER.
--   Requires Windows x64, REAPER 7.0 or newer, ReaImGui 0.9 or newer,
--   and the SWS Extension for full arrange-view drag-and-drop support.
-- @changelog
--   Kept file previews playing while dragging and inserting plug-ins.
--   Stopped FX insertion from raising the FX-chain window over floating plug-ins.
--   Added precise TCP/MCP FX-slot insertion, preserving empty mixer slots.
--   Fixed FX-slot insertion on tracks with no existing FX and kept batch order.
-- @metapackage
-- @provides
--   [win64 main] .
--   [win64] ReaBrowse_Canonical_Schema_v5.sql
--   [win64] sqlite3.exe
--   [win64] EULA.md
--   [win64] THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md
--   [win64] worker/publish/win-x64/ReaBrowseWorker.exe
--   [win64 extension] reaper_reabrowse_native_drag.dll

--[[
    ReaBrowse — Audio, MIDI, FX & Instrument Browser for REAPER
    - Perfect Timeline Sync & True Musical Loop Length calculation
    - Native timeline insertion (fixes length/tempo bugs, matches preview pitch/rate)
    - Flat-list search with folder scoping (Debounced + ListClipper Optimized)
    - Fully custom Left/Right/Up/Down Accordion folder-tree navigation (Single-click toggle)
    - Smart Drag & Drop to timeline (Retains Pitch, Key Sync, and Playrate settings)
    - Settings cog: Dark/Light presets, custom theme colors, font size
    - x2 / half-speed preview playback & manual +/-12st pitch shift (persistent)
    - Smart Heuristic Key Sync (Robust filename detection & Sysex Key Signatures)

    Auto Key/Sync was inspired in part by MX Tuner by
    Ilias-Timon Poulakis (FeedTheCat). The current implementation does not
    use MX Tuner's FFT pitch-detection algorithm.
    Use of ReaBrowse is governed by EULA.md.
    See THIRD_PARTY_NOTICES.md for attribution and license terms.
--]]

